      "id": 1,
      "text": "Belt, Montana began as a coal mining camp in 1877, named after nearby Belt Butte's girdle of rocks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitbelt.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Belt Museum, housed in the original town jail, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt%2C_Montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Belt was home to Montana's first coal mine, supplying fuel to Fort Benton during the early boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Belt Creek winds through the town, hosting minnows, suckers, and trout in the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
